-- title:
--   A uniform sign for U_q at minimal squarefree level
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal and with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$; let $p$ be an odd prime with $p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$ (a $2$-dimensional $k$-space with a monoid homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ to its endomorphisms, factoring through a finite level) which is absolutely irreducible, i.e. its base change to $\overline k$ is irreducible. Let $S$ be a finite set of primes containing $p$, and $N\ge 1$ an integer, nonzero, all of whose prime divisors lie in $S$, with $N$ squarefree; assume $\bar\rho$ is ramified at every prime $q\mid N$ with $q\ne p$ (some valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ over $q$ has an inertia element acting non-trivially), and that if $p\mid N$ then the adic representation [`GaloisRepAdic.ofResidualGaloisRep`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L196) $\bar\rho$ does not satisfy `IsFlatAt` at $p$ (no compatible system of finite flat cocommutative Hopf algebras over the localisation of $\mathbb Q$ at $p$ realising its finite-level quotients). Assume that the weight-two cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(N)$ have an integral structure, i.e. the $\mathbb C$-span of the lattice [`CuspForm.intLattice`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L3) $N\,2$ is everything. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) $N\,2\,S$ — the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}(S_2(\Gamma_0(N)))$ generated by the operators `heckeTLin` for primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, and `heckeULin` for primes $q\mid N$, $q\notin S$ — to $k$, such that for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit in $P$ and every $\sigma$ which is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $P$ (in the decomposition group and inducing $x\mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field), the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Finally let $q$ be a prime dividing $N$. The conclusion is that there is an integer $\varepsilon$ with $\varepsilon=1$ or $\varepsilon=-1$ such that for every characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation domain $\mathcal O'$ with finite residue field which is a finite $\mathcal O$-algebra by a local homomorphism, and every $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $\psi$ from [`CuspForm.heckeLocal`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) $N\,S\,\mathcal O\,\theta$ to $\mathcal O'$, there exists $s$ in [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) $N\,2\,S$ with $\psi(\pi(s))\ne 0$, where $\pi$ is the structure map to the local Hecke algebra, and with $U_q\circ s=\varepsilon\, s$ as endomorphisms of $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$, $U_q$ being [`CuspForm.heckeULin`](def/ModularForm_HeckeOperatorForms.html#L83) $2$ for $q\mid N$.
--
--   This is the cusp-form input to the statement that, at a squarefree minimal level, the operators $U_q$ for $q\mid N$ act by a single sign $\pm 1$ on the part of $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ seen by the localised Hecke algebra of the eigensystem $\theta$, in the form of a point-by-point witness $s$ not annihilated by the given point $\psi$ of the local algebra. It underlies the treatment of level structures in the modularity-lifting argument and is used in [`CuspForm.AuxLevel.exists_heckeTL_baseML_eq_smul_of_prime_dvd`](thm.html#CuspForm.AuxLevel.exists_heckeTL_baseML_eq_smul_of_prime_dvd).
